    {
      "id": "1574917510782918816",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-24T22:39:55.123+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": "2026-11-24T22:39:58.611+00:00",
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Yeah, I shorted the one on the end because I didn't want to change the wiring to/from the resistor. Originally there were in series. I put 7 in parallel and shortened them to 25.7u  so at ~ 330 ohm/sq  that should be (25.7 / 0.8) / 7 * 330 which is 1514 ohm nominal.",
      "author": {
        "id": "596068704471482370",
        "name": "246tnt",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "tnt",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/88d17af9d19ab43565b0c46751ef7d12-DFEE5.png"
